    "body": "# Qianqian v0.1.0 — First-Class TUI\n\nQianqian v0.1.0 is the first public release of the Windows first-class terminal music player.\n\nHighlights:\n\n- local-first playback from files and folders;\n- SongCore decode with native WASAPI output;\n- interactive Now Playing, Playlist, Audio and Visualizer views;\n- keyboard and mouse as equal interaction paths;\n- seek, volume, shuffle and repeat;\n- temporary playlist with distinct selection/current-playback state;\n- desired DSP controls for enable/bypass, preamp, presets and custom EQ;\n- truthful DSP boundary: applied state is not falsely reported;\n- live Spectrum, Peak/RMS and Waveform views from the Observation Plane;\n- responsive Wide / Normal / Compact / Minimum layouts;\n- portable Windows x86_64 package with no external runtime DLL requirement.\n\n## Supported package\n\n```text\nWindows x86_64\nportable zip\n```\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- no persistent media library/database;\n- no playlist-file import/export;\n- no lyrics, cover art or skins;\n- no gapless playback claim;\n- corrupt/unplayable-media policy remains future work (#231);\n- Visualizer cadence, richer color presentation and modal polish are tracked as post-v0.1.0 UX work (#233–#235).\n\nSHA-256:\n\n```text\n7918c3672a02075f7c01c38262116b1cdfaa776ea8caffb104695b9fd699ecb8\n```\n"
  },
